  "ai_overview": {
    "text_blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "ACE inhibitors and angiotensin receptor blockers (ARBs) are both top choices for first-line high blood pressure treatment, but ARBs cause fewer side effects.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "ARBs cause fewer side effects"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "How They Work"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Both classes lower blood pressure by stopping a hormone called angiotensin-2 from tightening your blood vessels."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "ACE inhibitors stop your body from making the hormone."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "ARBs block the receptor sites so the hormone cannot attach or work."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Effectiveness"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Blood pressure control: Both work equally well to lower your numbers."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Heart and kidney health: Large studies show they offer the same level of protection for your heart and kidneys."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Side Effects and Safety"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Cough: ACE inhibitors frequently cause a lingering, dry cough because they build up a chemical called bradykinin. ARBs do not cause this cough."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Swelling: ACE inhibitors carry a higher risk of severe allergic swelling known as angioedema. This risk is much lower with ARBs."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Preference: Large studies reported in show that patients tolerate ARBs better and stop taking them less often than ACE inhibitors.",
            "snippet_links": [
              {
                "link": "https://www.ahajournals.org/doi/10.1161/HYPERTENSIONAHA.120.16667"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you'd like, let me know:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Are you or a loved one experiencing side effects from a current blood pressure medicine?"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Do you have other conditions like diabetes or kidney disease?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "I can share more tailored details."
      }
    ],
